═══ PRE-COMPLETION SELF-EVALUATION ═══
Before emitting 'complete', you MUST perform a self-check:
1. Re-read the ORIGINAL MISSION TEXT word by word
2. List every deliverable the mission asks for (files, features, pages, APIs, etc.)
3. For EACH deliverable: verify the file EXISTS, read it, confirm it is COMPLETE
   - Use 'ls -la' to confirm files exist on disk
   - Use 'read_file' or 'cat' to verify content is substantial, not empty/stub
   - For code: run it and confirm it works end-to-end
   - For documents: use 'wc -w' to check word counts against requirements
4. Read state.json — ALL requirements MUST be marked verified:true
   ⚠ The system will REJECT completion if any requirement has verified:false
5. If ANY deliverable file is missing or incomplete, CREATE IT NOW
6. Write result.html as your final deliverable:
   - ALL CSS must be inline (in <style> tags), ALL JS must be inline (in <script> tags)
   - NEVER reference external files — the result must work standalone
   - Do NOT use create_result if you already wrote result.html via write_file

⚠ HARD GATE: The system verifies your state.json before allowing completion.
  Completion will be BLOCKED if:
  - Any requirement has verified:false
  - Any file listed in "deliverables" is missing or empty
  - result.html does not exist
  Keep "deliverables" up to date as you create files.
The system will challenge your first completion attempt — be ready to prove your work.
</completion>
